<title>BELGIUM: EU's deSilguy - budget policies must be credible.</title>
<headline>EU's deSilguy - budget policies must be credible.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Commissioner Yves-Thibault de Silguy said on Wednesday that one-off budgetary measures designed to meet the Maastricht treaty's budget criteria would not pre-empt the move towards monetary union.</p>
<p>Speaking at a news conference, de Silguy said non-repetitive operations, such as France's decision to use the proceeds from the privatisation of France Telecom to lower its deficit, would have to be followed by durable budget policies.</p>
<p>&quot;One-off measures do not pre-empt the decision to move to the third stage of monetary union,&quot; de Silguy said.</p>
</text>
